# destructor-without-override (#5): a class-declaration destructor with no
# virtual-family directive hides the inherited (virtual) destructor and leaks.
# Fires on the declaration 'destructor Destroy;' (line 6, no override); NOT on the
# one with 'override' (line 10) nor on the implementation defProc (line 13 --
# 'override' belongs on the declaration, not the impl).
destructor-without-override 6
!destructor-without-override 10
!destructor-without-override 13
